Implemented a structural, per-floor camera fit. The old bounds combined architectural geometry with decorative furniture, label padding, and broad exterior zones, so outliers could push the camera too far back. The new fit uses room outlines, circulation, doors, stairs, entrance features, and floor extensions; it excludes those outliers and keeps furniture as a fallback for floors without structural geometry. Entrance features use their authored attachment positions.

The existing three-quarter angle, safe-viewport centering, and intentional entry/floor-switch refits remain. I did not change Follow tracking or route progress behavior.

### Changes

- [IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx#L1490) now uses the structural floor bounds.
- [indoor3dGeometry.ts](src/lib/indoor3dGeometry.ts#L239) calculates bounds from authored room and circulation geometry.
- [indoor3dGeometry.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/indoor3dGeometry.test.ts#L347) covers compact, large, rectangular, irregular, and decoration-heavy floors, plus entrance attachment framing.

### Verification

- **PASS:** 4 focused camera and floor-switching test files; 80 tests.
- **PASS:** Production build. Vite still reports existing large chunks over 500 kB.
