**CEIT mobile framing is fixed.** The mobile camera now turns elongated floors farther toward screen height and gives compact or square floors a modest portrait adjustment. Camera elevation stays the same; desktop framing is unchanged. The renderer applies this fit to ordinary indoor views, leaving Follow, Discover, and route-preview camera ownership intact.

The cause was the portrait camera angle: elongated floors kept too much side yaw, while compact floors got no portrait adjustment. Both could make the model look small on a tall screen. CANTEEN’s measured camera distance was 33.6, above the 4.5 minimum, so its remaining whitespace came from its compact shape, not a distance clamp. The updated geometry logic and tests are in [indoor3dGeometry.ts](src/lib/indoor3dGeometry.ts#L216) and [indoor3dGeometry.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/indoor3dGeometry.test.ts#L368). The existing renderer gate and safe-viewport calculation are in [IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx#L1795) and [student3dCameraFocus.ts](src/lib/student3dCameraFocus.ts#L131).

### Chromium verification

Chrome 155 rendered CEIT Ground Floor at **320×568, 360×640, 390×844, 430×932, 768×1024, and 1440×900**. WebGL contexts remained live and there were no browser errors. CABA, COED, Student Center, and CANTEEN also rendered at 390×844. I switched CEIT to Floor 2, toggled 2D and 3D, and checked light mode at 390×844.

![CEIT Ground Floor at 390×844](verification-artifacts/indoor-camera-fit-390x844.png)

Additional captures: [CEIT desktop 1440×900](verification-artifacts/indoor-camera-fit-1440x900.png), [CEIT Floor 2](verification-artifacts/indoor-camera-fit-ceit-floor2-390x844.png), [light theme](verification-artifacts/indoor-camera-fit-ceit-light-390x844.png), [CABA](verification-artifacts/indoor-camera-fit-caba-390x844.png), [COED](verification-artifacts/indoor-camera-fit-coed-390x844.png), [Student Center](verification-artifacts/indoor-camera-fit-sc-390x844.png), and [CANTEEN](verification-artifacts/indoor-camera-fit-can-390x844.png).

### Checks and remaining notes

- **PASS:** 88 focused tests across five files; production build; `git diff --check`.
- **TypeScript:** baseline comparison found 1,022 diagnostics before and 1,025 now. The three additional diagnostics are in the unrelated, already-edited [campusService.publish.test.ts](src/services/__tests__/campusService.publish.test.ts); none are in the camera-fit files. The build also retains its large-chunk warning.
- At 320px, some long floating room-name labels reach or clip at the screen edge. The floor geometry, stairs, and exits remain visible.
- Compact floors such as CANTEEN naturally leave more vertical space because their footprint is square in a portrait viewport. Other campuses and a Guided Follow route were not manually exercised in Chromium this pass; the fit remains geometry-driven, and Follow is excluded by the renderer gate.
