![CEIT Ground Floor at 1440×900](verification-artifacts/camera-stability-20261021/final-ceit-ground-1440x900.png)

## Checks and limitations

**PASS:** 344 focused camera/navigation tests across 12 files; 35 SOS workflow tests across 2 files; production build; `git diff --check`.

**TypeScript baseline comparison: FAIL overall.** `tsc --noEmit` still reports repository diagnostics. Compared with the saved baseline, 5 diagnostic identities were added and 3 resolved, in publication tests and database generic casts; none were in the camera/navigation files. The build also reports existing large chunks over 500 kB.

Chromium logged repeated Three.js “Context Lost” messages during renderer replacements. The active canvas reported its context was healthy and continued rendering; no FPS improvement is claimed.

The camera implementation and regressions are in [IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx), [indoor3dGeometry.ts](src/lib/indoor3dGeometry.ts), [student3dCameraFocus.ts](src/lib/student3dCameraFocus.ts), [CampusMapPage.tsx](src/pages/CampusMapPage.tsx), and their focused tests in [indoor3dGeometry.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/indoor3dGeometry.test.ts) and [student3dCameraFocus.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/student3dCameraFocus.test.ts). The resumed check made no source edits. Shared worktree changes remain intact; nothing was committed, pushed or deployed.
