## Result

**The recovery path now preserves the saved Follow camera offset and reattaches it to the canonical route marker.** The original Start Navigation framing defaults were left unchanged.

### Cause and fix

Resume recovery could create a new camera pose instead of retaining the current Follow view. Indoor recovery could derive distance from the whole floor’s `halfDepth`, pulling the camera far away; outdoor recovery used a fixed 12-unit pose, losing the user’s orbit.

The fix captures camera position relative to its orbit target—preserving distance and orientation—and stores it by campus or building/floor context. Recovery reads the canonical route cursor and marker, uses the bookmark for that context, and clamps it to the active renderer’s limits. A new scene without a bookmark gets its own scene-specific Follow framing, rather than a whole-floor overview. Stale recovery requests are checked against their context and nonce. The changes are in [CampusMapPage.tsx](src/pages/CampusMapPage.tsx#L1009), [IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx#L2001), [StudentCampus3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/StudentCampus3DRenderer.tsx#L2100), [student3dCameraPose.ts](src/lib/student3dCameraPose.ts), and [student3dCameraRecenter.ts](src/lib/student3dCameraRecenter.ts).

Camera pose capture is event-driven; it does not add per-frame React updates. Ordinary Pause/Resume keeps the current camera in place. When recovery is needed after inspection, it returns to the canonical route context and restores that context’s saved framing. Actual stair/elevator Continue handoffs remain intact.

### Verification

- **Automated tests — PASS:** 6 focused files, 153 tests passed. Camera-pose tests cover retained distance and orientation, context-specific bookmarks, clamping, and repeated recovery without cumulative zoom drift. See [student3dCameraPose.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/student3dCameraPose.test.ts) and [student3dCameraRecenter.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/student3dCameraRecenter.test.ts).
- **Standard route — PASS:** In Chromium at 1440×900, Campus Gate → COED 301 produced an 11-step route through CANTEEN, COED Ground Floor, and an elevator handoff to Floor 3. I paused on COED Ground Floor step 8, resumed to the elevator step, continued to Floor 3, and reached automatic arrival at COED 301.
- **Pause/Resume interaction — PASS, visual scale NOT VERIFIED:** At 1440×900 and 390×844, the route stayed in Follow, retained its step while paused, accepted a wheel event while paused, then resumed along the route. The 390×844 run continued to the entrance handoff.
- **Renderer switch — PASS for route state:** At 430×932, switching 3D → 2D → 3D preserved the current route step and entrance handoff. After remount, however, the WebGL canvas remained at its 300×150 placeholder size, so camera interaction at that viewport was **NOT VERIFIED**.
- **Accessible and SOS browser routes — NOT VERIFIED:** The live route exercise used Standard only. The shared camera recovery helpers are mode-independent, but I did not run Accessible or SOS flows.
