## A. Bottleneck found

**PASS — Confirmed:** On the outdoor Student Map, the page statically imported the indoor floor artwork module to use its viewport calculation. That made indoor rendering code load before a student opened a building. The production Chromium waterfall showed the floor artwork chunk at **224 KB decoded / 61.7 KB transferred** on the initial outdoor map.

**NOT VERIFIED:** I found no measured evidence tying the reported Builder dragging or sidebar lag to a particular computation. The Admin Builder route redirects to sign-in in this browser session, so I did not bypass authentication or claim to have profiled it.

## B. Improvement implemented

I moved the existing floor viewport calculation into a small utility, kept its existing export available, and made the Student Map load the floor artwork only when entering a building. A local SVG loading message keeps the map page and controls mounted while that module loads.

The initial production map transferred **18,794 fewer JavaScript bytes** in this Chromium run: **811,108 bytes before → 792,314 after**, across 19 script resources (**2.3% less**). The common canvas asset code remains loaded because the outdoor map uses it; the floor scene and floor-ordering chunks are deferred until a building is entered.

This is a measured initial-load reduction. It does **not** establish better FPS, frame pacing, or low-end-device performance.

## C. Performance findings

The Student Map’s main chunk remains large at **1,181 KB minified / 321 KB gzip**. The build also reports large chunks for the Admin Builder (**1,905 KB / 507 KB gzip**), the app index (**924 KB / 270 KB gzip**), and 3D input (**861 KB / 232 KB gzip**). The Vite large-chunk warning remains.

The browser run used a viewport of **839×811 at DPR 1.25**. I did not have CPU throttling or a real low-end Android or older laptop profile. Memory-growth and comparable before/after frame-time measurements were unavailable.

## D. Functionality and verification

**PASS — Build:** `pnpm build` succeeded. The large-chunk warning remains.

**PASS — Tests:** All **239 focused tests passed** across 12 files: 77 Student Map and floor-scene tests, 152 routing and emergency-navigation tests, and 10 Builder camera/performance tests. The first 77-test group also passed before the change.

**PASS — TypeScript baseline comparison:** `tsc --noEmit` still exits with errors: **1,018 diagnostics before and after**. There were no new file/code diagnostic groups; the new viewport utility has no diagnostics. TypeScript is not clean.

**PASS — Chromium interactions:** In the local production build, I switched to 3D, entered Student Center, switched to the 2D floor view, selected Floor 2, and returned to the outdoor map. The floor views displayed rooms, furniture, stairs, and exit markings. The indoor chunk loaded on building entry.

**NOT VERIFIED — 3D lifecycle:** Chromium logged two `THREE.WebGLRenderer: Context Lost` messages during 3D transitions. The tested map returned to 2D and remained usable, but this run cannot distinguish expected renderer disposal from a longer-session WebGL stability issue. Visual fidelity and repeated-session memory behavior were not measured.

**BLOCKED — Admin Builder browser profiling:** The route requires an authorized session and redirected to sign-in. No authentication was bypassed.

`git diff --check` passed, the conflict-marker scan found none, and the existing Vite dev server still returned HTTP 200. I did not run the full Vitest suite. No save/publish, route algorithm, geometry, persistence, or production-data code was changed.

## E. Remaining opportunities

The Student Map and Admin Builder chunks still warrant an import-graph review. Builder interaction profiling and real low-end device measurements should come first; no renderer, camera, or adaptive-quality changes were justified by this evidence.

## F. Files changed in this pass

The shared worktree already contained other uncommitted changes; I preserved them. This pass changed only:

- [CampusMapPage.tsx](src/pages/CampusMapPage.tsx#L103) — deferred indoor scene loading and local fallback.
- [ReadonlyFloorPlanVisuals.tsx](src/components/map-builder/ReadonlyFloorPlanVisuals.tsx#L45) — retained exports while moving the viewport utility.
- [readonlyFloorPlanViewport.ts](src/components/map-builder/readonlyFloorPlanViewport.ts) — contains the unchanged viewport calculation.

**Overall: PASS for the focused payload optimization and tested Student Map transitions. NOT VERIFIED for low-end performance, Admin Builder runtime performance, 3D long-session stability, and broad FPS improvement.**
