## 1. Root cause

**PASS — test synchronization issue, not a reproduced application race.** Under combined test load, jsdom’s native `requestAnimationFrame` timestamp and Node’s global `performance.now()` were on different time origins. A captured frame was about **3.19 seconds behind** the performance clock, exceeding the tests’ existing 3-second recovery assertion window.

The animation continued receiving frames. I observed no cancellation or lost completion callback. In a browser, RAF timestamps and `performance.now()` share a clock; the mismatch was specific to the test environment.

## 2. Change made

I changed only the Student Map test harness to pass RAF callbacks timestamps from the same performance clock the camera code uses. I added a small assertion that checks those timestamps stay aligned. The existing route recovery tests remain intact and continue to assert the expected UI state; no timeout was extended.

No application camera or navigation code changed. The shared renderer mock changes already present in the test file were preserved.

